---
description: Register nested CommandBase subcommands; never branch on args[0] in _cmd handlers
globs: civcraft/src/main/java/com/avrgaming/civcraft/ui/command/**/*.java
alwaysApply: false
---

# Nested subcommands on CommandBase

When a command has distinct actions (e.g. `res` vs `res intro`), **register each action** in `init()` via `commands.put(...)`, either as a `*_cmd()` method or a nested `CommandBase` (`Supplier::new`).

## Do this

```java
// Parent: AdminQuestCommand
this.commands.put("res", "Resident quest admin.", AdminQuestResidentCommand::new);

// Child: AdminQuestResidentCommand
this.commands.put("intro", "[resident] - Start intro cinematic.", residents());

public void intro_cmd() throws CivException {
    Resident target = this.getNamedResidentOrSelf(1);
    // ...
}
```

Use `sendUnknownToDefault = true` when the default action should handle a **free argument** (e.g. `/ad quest res <resident>`) after registered subcommands are checked.

## Do not do this

```java
// ❌ BAD — manual subcommand dispatch inside one _cmd
public void res_cmd() throws CivException {
    if (this.args.length >= 2 && "intro".equalsIgnoreCase(this.args[1])) {
        this.startIntro(...);
        return;
    }
    // ...
}
```

## Routing rules

- **Nested class** (`AdminQuestResidentCommand::new`): use for a whole branch (`/ad quest res …`).
- **`*_cmd()` on the same class**: use for leaf actions (`intro_cmd`, `open_cmd`).
- **Never** compare `args[1]`, `args[2]`, … to subcommand names when those names could be registered instead.
